<% content_for :title, "Slate — #{@slate.name}" %>

<style>
  /* FILL vs INK, per series. Each formula series has ONE brand colour that
     paints its graphics — the chart stroke, the panel's border-left, the
     sliders' accent-color — and those are graphical objects, whose bar is WCAG
     1.4.11's 3:1 rather than 4.5:1. The same colour also paints the panel's
     small mono values, and small TEXT owes 4.5:1. Three of the four series
     cannot do both jobs with one hex, so each keeps its fill and gets an -ink
     for text.

     EVERY FILL CLEARS THE 3:1 BAR ON THIS CARD, IN BOTH THEMES. Three of the
     four did not, measured here: --fc-goals 1.96:1 light, --fc-dk-score 2.22:1
     dark, --fc-dk-total 2.78:1 light; only --fc-mult cleared both (3.10 / 3.60).
     Each failing theme now takes a raised fill and the PASSING theme is
     untouched, so a series keeps its brand colour wherever it already cleared.
     The ink work below is UNCHANGED: the inks answer small TEXT at 4.5:1, a
     different bar, and a fill that clears 3:1 does not make its ink redundant.

     THE GROUND IS THE CARD, VERIFIED rather than assumed. The chart's canvas and
     all three variable panels are `bg-surface border border-subtle rounded-lg
     p-4`, and bg-surface compiles to var(--color-surface). The two Save Formula
     buttons name no surface of their own, so their `border-color: var(--fc-dk-score)`
     sits on the PAGE — measured separately below and asserted separately.

     --fc-mult IS THE THIN ONE, deliberately left alone. It is 3.10:1 on the light
     card, over the bar with 0.10 to spare, and 2.96:1 on the light PAGE, which it
     never sits on. Raising it would move the brand violet itself, which was Mr.
     McRitchie's call on 2026-09-21 and is not this task's to reopen.

     ONLY THE FAILING THEME MOVES. A series that already clears as text in one
     theme keeps its own brand colour there, so the tie between a number and
     its chart line stays exact wherever it can:

       --fc-goals      dark  #B8B0FF  5.68:1 card — unchanged, it cleared
                       light #6558E5  5.15:1 card (was #B8B0FF, 1.96:1)
                                      The brand ramp's violet-600 — a NAMED shade,
                                      not a fresh hex — and 1.66:1 from --fc-mult,
                                      so the two violet chart lines stay apart.
                                      Darkening #B8B0FF toward grey instead reached
                                      3.25:1 at only 1.05:1 from --fc-mult: over the
                                      bar and useless. Identity is measured here,
                                      not eyeballed.
       --fc-goals-ink  dark  #B8B0FF ................. 5.68:1 (the series itself)
                       light var(--color-violet-ink) . 6.03:1 (#5B50CE)

       --fc-dk-score      light #15803D  5.02:1 card — unchanged, it cleared
                          dark  #3AA757  3.64:1 card (was #15803D, 2.22:1)
                                         and 5.69:1 on the PAGE, the ground of the
                                         two Save Formula buttons' border-color.

     THE TWO DARK GREENS CANNOT BE SEPARATED BY LUMINANCE, and that is physics
     rather than a shortcut. --fc-dk-score and --fc-dk-total must BOTH clear 3:1
     on the same dark card, which forces both into one luminance band: measured
     over nine candidate greens, the best separation from --fc-dk-total that
     still clears the floor is 1.27:1 (#359B52, floor 3.17), against 1.10:1 for
     the #3AA757 chosen here (floor 3.64). Neither gap is perceptible, so the
     thicker floor margin wins. What keeps them apart is not luminance: they
     never appear as adjacent marks — DK Score is a variable PANEL with its own
     heading and sliders, DK Expectation is a CHART line with its own legend
     entry. Do not "fix" the 1.10 by lowering a fill back under the bar.
       --fc-dk-score-ink  light #15803D ................... 5.02:1 (the series itself)
                          dark  var(--color-primary-ink) .. 5.54:1 card (#81C784)

       --fc-dk-total   dark  #4BAF50  4.01:1 card — unchanged, it cleared
                       light #3E9E43  3.40:1 card (was #4BAF50, 2.78:1)
                                      Graphics-only in the DOM, so it has no -ink.
                                      It DOES paint the chart's DK axis title and
                                      tick labels, which are CANVAS text at 11px and
                                      owe 4.5:1 — out of this guard's reach and
                                      recorded in docs/FORMULAS.md, not fixed here.

     THE DARK GREEN HAS A SECOND GROUND TO CLEAR. Two Save Formula buttons
     paint this token as text while naming no surface of their own, so they sit
     on the layout body's bg-page: 3.48:1 before, 8.68:1 on --color-primary-ink.
     A fix scoped to the three panels would have left them.

     BOTH BORROWED INKS ARE THIS APP'S OWN TOKENS, NOT THE RESOLVER'S. They are
     declared in app/assets/tailwind/application.css — Studio::ThemeResolver
     emits neither --color-primary-ink nor --color-violet-ink (it emits
     --color-primary and its scale, plus the danger, warning and success inks).
     So NONE of the four values above tracks a theme change; until 2026-09-22
     this comment said they were "DERIVED per theme by Studio::ThemeResolver",
     and that was false. Borrowing them is still the right design — they move
     with the ink tokens the rest of the app already reads, instead of adding a
     fourth pinned pair here — it just is not the reason that was written down.
     "control: the borrowed inks are the app's, not the resolver's" in the guard
     asserts this, so the claim reds if it stops being true.

     WHAT THE THEME DOES MOVE IS THE GROUND. The four surfaces ARE
     resolver-derived, so changing the dark base shifts every ratio above while
     these inks stay pinned. The guard catches that by reddening.

     Same selector convention as the engine's theme block and as
     --color-violet-ink in app/assets/tailwind/application.css, so a .dark
     container inside a light page flips these with the rest of the theme.

     Guard: test/views/violet_text_contrast_test.rb resolves every inline
     `color:` on this page through these tokens and measures it against the
     surface the element actually sits on, so editing a hex here without
     re-measuring fails the suite. */
  :root {
    --fc-mult: #8E82FE;
    --fc-mult-ink: var(--color-violet-ink);
  }
  :root,
  .dark {
    --fc-goals: #B8B0FF;
    --fc-dk-score: #3AA757;
    --fc-dk-total: #4BAF50;
    --fc-goals-ink: #B8B0FF;
    --fc-dk-score-ink: var(--color-primary-ink);
  }
  html:not(.dark) {
    --fc-goals: #6558E5;
    --fc-dk-score: #15803D;
    --fc-dk-total: #3E9E43;
    --fc-goals-ink: var(--color-violet-ink);
    --fc-dk-score-ink: #15803D;
  }
</style>

<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.7/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
<script>
  // THE CHART READS THE FILL TOKENS; IT DOES NOT KEEP A COPY OF THEM.
  //
  // This was three hex literals under a comment calling itself "single source
  // of truth", while the <style> block above declared the same three colours.
  // There were two sources, and this was the copy. That was survivable while
  // the fills were theme-independent. It is not now: --fc-goals, --fc-dk-score
  // and --fc-dk-total each take a different value per theme, so a literal here
  // paints the wrong theme's colour — and nothing would say so, because a
  // canvas stroke is not reachable from the static scan that measures an
  // inline `style:`.
  //
  // Read at BUILD time, not at parse time: the MutationObserver at the foot of
  // this script rebuilds the chart when <html>'s class list flips, and that is
  // what carries a per-theme fill onto the canvas at all.
  //
  // NO HEX FALLBACK, on purpose — a fallback is the copy this removes. The
  // guard asserts the page declares all four tokens as 6-digit hexes in both
  // themes, which is also what keeps the `+ '14'` alpha suffix below a valid
  // 8-digit #RRGGBBAA instead of a silently malformed colour.
  function _fcColors() {
    var style = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
    var read = function(name) { return style.getPropertyValue(name).trim(); };
    return {
      mult:    read('--fc-mult'),      // Turf Score (violet)
      goals:   read('--fc-goals'),     // Goals Distribution (violet, per theme)
      dkTotal: read('--fc-dk-total')   // DK Expectation (green, per theme)
    };
  }

  <%# Charted per TEAM, not per matchup row — a three-week slate would otherwise
      plot 96 points for 32 teams and rank each team three times. per_game is
      the team's expected points PER GAME, which is what it is ranked on (on a
      one-week slate that is simply its one game). game_factor picks the line
      it prices on: 1.0 for a full-span team, 1.5 for a team with a bye inside a
      three-week span (Slate "Two lines"). %>
  var _fcMatchups = <%== @team_rows.map { |row|
    {
      rank: row.rank,
      emoji: row.team.emoji,
      team: row.team.name,
      short: row.team.short_name,
      opponent: row.matchups.filter_map { |m| m.opponent_team&.short_name }.join(" / "),
      turf_score: row.turf_score&.to_f,
      team_total: row.expected_points,
      per_game: row.expected_points_per_game.round(2),
      games: row.matchups.size,
      game_factor: row.game_factor
    }
  }.to_json %>;
  var FC_TWO_LINES = _fcMatchups.some(function(m) { return m.game_factor > 1; });
  // A span ranks on points PER GAME, so that is what the DK line plots.
  var FC_DK_AXIS = _fcMatchups.some(function(m) { return m.games > 1; }) ? 'DK per game' : 'DK Total';

  var _fcChart = null;

  // THE PRICES, COMPUTED IN RUBY — one per slider position, per line, per rank.
  //
  // This used to be a JavaScript copy of the curve, and a copy of a rounding
  // rule is a second rule: Ruby rounds a tie away from zero on the decimal,
  // `toFixed` rounds the binary double, and on an exact tie they disagree. That
  // mattered because "Save Multipliers" posts the text ON SCREEN, so the page
  // could write a price the curve never produced. Measured before the fix over
  // both curves, n 2-48, all 21 slider positions and game factors 1.0/1.5/1.25:
  // 314 of 148,050 cells disagreed (309 nfl, 5 fifa). The NFL board was clean
  // because the NFL CURVE is clean at n=32 — not because nothing diverged
  // there: all five fifa cells sit at n=32, which is a World Cup group stage
  // as readily as it is an NFL season.
  //
  // The slider has 21 positions (0..10 step 0.5), so the whole space fits in
  // the page and the browser never computes a price again — it looks one up.
  var FC_SPORT = '<%= @slate.sport %>';
  var _fcPrices = <%== turf_score_scale_table(slate: @slate, teams: @team_rows.size,
                                              factors: @team_rows.map(&:game_factor),
                                              resolved_scale: @slate.resolved_formula[:formula_mult_scale]).to_json %>;

  function _fcMult(rank, N, multScale, gameFactor) {
    var byScale = _fcPrices[(multScale || 0).toFixed(1)];
    var line = byScale && byScale[(gameFactor || 1.0).toFixed(1)];
    var price = line && line[rank - 1];
    // No silent fallback to a recomputed value: a missing cell means the table
    // and the board disagree about the slate, and inventing a number here is
    // how the second implementation would grow back.
    return price === undefined || price === null ? null : price;
  }

  function _fcCompute(A, lineExp, probExp, multBase, multScale, goalBase, goalScale) {
    var N = _fcMatchups.length;
    var lnN = Math.log(N);
    return _fcMatchups.map(function(m, i) {
      var rank = i + 1;
      return {
        emoji: m.emoji, team: m.team, opponent: m.opponent, rank: rank,
        mult: _fcMult(rank, N, multScale, m.game_factor),
        goals: Math.round((goalBase + goalScale * Math.log(N / rank) / lnN) * 100) / 100,
        teamTotal: m.per_game,
        games: m.games,
        twoLine: m.game_factor > 1
      };
    });
  }

  // NFL axis windows: shrink the DK axis to the data (visual fidelity), then
  // derive the reversed Turf window LINEARLY from it so turf 1.0 maps to the
  // same pixel as the DK maximum — both lines leave the same point, and the
  // x2 top lands on the DK minimum's pixel. Returns null when the mapping is
  // undefined (no DK data, or a flat DK line) — callers fall back to static
  // windows.
  function _fcNflAxisWindows(data, multScale) {
    if (FC_SPORT !== 'nfl') return null;
    var dkVals = data.map(function(d) { return d.teamTotal; }).filter(function(v) { return v !== null && v !== undefined; });
    if (dkVals.length < 2) return null;
    var dkMax = Math.max.apply(null, dkVals);
    var dkMin = Math.min.apply(null, dkVals);
    if (dkMax === dkMin) return null;
    // ~one extra deviation of margin: the lines float inside the window
    // (e.g. 50-85 / 0.8-2.2 on a 54-81 spread) instead of touching its edges.
    var pad = Math.max(2, (dkMax - dkMin) * 0.13);
    var y2Min = Math.floor(dkMin - pad);
    var y2Max = Math.ceil(dkMax + pad);
    // The two-game line tops out at 1.5x the curve, below the DK minimum's
    // pixel. Stretch the DK axis DOWN until the highest multiplier fits, so the
    // turf-1.0-at-DK-max anchoring still holds and the bye line stays on chart.
    var multMax = Math.max.apply(null, data.map(function(d) { return d.mult; }));
    var neededY2Min = dkMax - (multMax + 0.15 - 1) * (dkMax - dkMin) / multScale;
    if (multScale > 0 && neededY2Min < y2Min) y2Min = Math.floor(neededY2Min);
    var tMin = 1 - multScale * (y2Max - dkMax) / (dkMax - dkMin);
    var tMax = tMin + multScale * (y2Max - y2Min) / (dkMax - dkMin);
    return { y2Min: y2Min, y2Max: y2Max, tMin: tMin, tMax: tMax };
  }

  function _fcBuildChart(data) {
    var canvas = document.getElementById('formulaCurvesChart');
    if (!canvas) return;
    var existing = Chart.getChart(canvas);
    if (existing) existing.destroy();
    var windows = _fcNflAxisWindows(data, _fcSliders.multScale);

    var FC = _fcColors();
    var isDark = document.documentElement.classList.contains('dark');
    var gridColor = isDark ? 'rgba(255,255,255,0.08)' : 'rgba(0,0,0,0.08)';
    var textColor = isDark ? 'rgba(255,255,255,0.5)' : 'rgba(0,0,0,0.5)';

    // Two lines on a bye span: full-span teams on the usual curve, bye teams on
    // the 1.5x line. Each dataset skips the other's teams (null + spanGaps), so
    // each draws as its own line across the one shared ranking.
    var datasets = [
      {
        label: 'Turf Score',
        data: data.map(function(d) { return d.twoLine ? null : d.mult; }),
        borderColor: FC.mult,
        backgroundColor: FC.mult + '14',
        borderWidth: 2.5, pointRadius: 2, pointHoverRadius: 6, tension: 0.3, fill: false, yAxisID: 'y', spanGaps: true, order: 1
      }
    ];
    if (FC_TWO_LINES) {
      datasets.push({
        label: 'Turf Score · bye line',
        data: data.map(function(d) { return d.twoLine ? d.mult : null; }),
        borderColor: FC.mult,
        backgroundColor: FC.mult,
        borderWidth: 2, borderDash: [2, 3], pointRadius: 4, pointHoverRadius: 7, tension: 0, fill: false, yAxisID: 'y', spanGaps: true, order: 1
      });
    }
    // Goals are a soccer concept — on NFL slates the series is noise.
    if (FC_SPORT !== 'nfl') {
      datasets.push({
        label: 'Goals Distribution',
        data: data.map(function(d) { return d.goals; }),
        borderColor: FC.goals,
        backgroundColor: FC.goals + '14',
        borderWidth: 2, borderDash: [6, 3], pointRadius: 2, pointHoverRadius: 6, tension: 0.3, fill: false, yAxisID: 'y', order: 2
      });
    }
    datasets.push({
      label: 'DK Expectation',
      data: data.map(function(d) { return d.teamTotal; }),
      borderColor: FC.dkTotal,
      backgroundColor: FC.dkTotal + '14',
      borderWidth: 1.5, borderDash: [6, 3], pointRadius: 2, pointHoverRadius: 6, tension: 0.3, fill: false, yAxisID: 'y2', spanGaps: true, order: 3
    });

    _fcChart = new Chart(canvas, {
      type: 'line',
      data: {
        labels: data.map(function(d) { return d.emoji; }),
        datasets: datasets
      },
      options: {
        responsive: true, maintainAspectRatio: false,
        interaction: { mode: 'index', intersect: false },
        plugins: {
          legend: { labels: { color: textColor, font: { size: 11 }, usePointStyle: true, pointStyle: 'line' } },
          tooltip: {
            backgroundColor: isDark ? 'rgba(20,18,40,0.95)' : 'rgba(255,255,255,0.95)',
            titleColor: isDark ? '#fff' : '#111',
            bodyColor: isDark ? 'rgba(255,255,255,0.8)' : 'rgba(0,0,0,0.7)',
            borderColor: isDark ? 'rgba(255,255,255,0.1)' : 'rgba(0,0,0,0.1)',
            borderWidth: 1, padding: 12, displayColors: true,
            callbacks: {
              title: function(items) {
                var d = _fcLastData[items[0].dataIndex];
                return d.emoji + ' ' + d.team + ' vs ' + (d.opponent || '—');
              },
              afterTitle: function(items) {
                var d = _fcLastData[items[0].dataIndex];
                // `mult` is null when the price table has no cell for this
                // scale; the tooltip says so rather than throwing on hover.
                var mult = d.mult === null || d.mult === undefined ? '—' : 'x' + d.mult.toFixed(1);
                return 'Rank #' + d.rank + '  ·  Turf Score ' + mult + (d.twoLine ? '  ·  ' + d.games + ' games (bye line)' : '');
              },
              label: function(ctx) {
                var val = ctx.parsed.y;
                if (val === null || val === undefined) return null;
                return '  ' + ctx.dataset.label + ': ' + val.toFixed(2);
              }
            }
          }
        },
        scales: {
          x: { ticks: { color: textColor, font: { size: 14 }, maxRotation: 0, minRotation: 0, autoSkip: true, maxTicksLimit: 48 }, grid: { color: gridColor } },
          // DK Total owns the LEFT axis and auto-scales to the data — an NFL
          // span slate reads ~0-85 while a World Cup goals slate reads ~0-5.
          // The old config bound DK Expectation to the 0-5 Turf axis, drawing
          // an 81-point total off-chart while a hardcoded 0-5 "DK Total" axis
          // mirrored uselessly on the right. Axis text wears the series green
          // so the accurate scale reads as the green line's.
          y2: windows
            ? { position: 'left', title: { display: true, text: FC_DK_AXIS, color: FC.dkTotal, font: { size: 11 } }, ticks: { color: FC.dkTotal }, grid: { drawOnChartArea: false }, min: windows.y2Min, max: windows.y2Max }
            : { position: 'left', title: { display: true, text: FC_DK_AXIS, color: FC.dkTotal, font: { size: 11 } }, ticks: { color: FC.dkTotal }, grid: { drawOnChartArea: false }, beginAtZero: true },
          // NFL: reversed so x1.0 sits at the TOP — the Turf line then falls
          // with rank alongside the DK Expectation line instead of crossing it,
          // and the window derived by _fcNflAxisWindows anchors turf 1.0 to the
          // DK maximum's pixel so both lines leave the same point.
          y: windows
            ? { position: 'right', reverse: true, title: { display: true, text: 'Turf Score', color: textColor, font: { size: 11 } }, ticks: { color: textColor }, grid: { color: gridColor }, min: windows.tMin, max: windows.tMax }
            : { position: 'right', reverse: FC_SPORT === 'nfl', title: { display: true, text: 'Turf Score', color: textColor, font: { size: 11 } }, ticks: { color: textColor }, grid: { color: gridColor }, min: 0, max: 5 }
        }
      }
    });
  }

  var _fcLastData = [];

  // Store current slider values for rankManager to use after drag
  // Initialize from DB-resolved formula (slate → default slate → hardcoded)
  var _fcDefaults = <%== @slate.resolved_formula.to_json %>;
  var _fcSliders = {
    A: _fcDefaults.formula_a,
    lineExp: _fcDefaults.formula_line_exp,
    probExp: _fcDefaults.formula_prob_exp,
    multBase: _fcDefaults.formula_mult_base,
    // One decimal, rounded in RUBY, so the only scales this page can hold are
    // ones the price table has a key for — the slider's half-steps, or this.
    multScale: <%= price_key(@slate.resolved_formula[:formula_mult_scale]) %>,
    goalBase: _fcDefaults.formula_goal_base,
    goalScale: _fcDefaults.formula_goal_scale
  };

  function _fcUpdate(A, lineExp, probExp, multBase, multScale, goalBase, goalScale) {
    _fcSliders = { A: A, lineExp: lineExp, probExp: probExp, multBase: multBase, multScale: multScale, goalBase: goalBase, goalScale: goalScale };
    var data = _fcCompute(A, lineExp, probExp, multBase, multScale, goalBase, goalScale);
    _fcLastData = data;
    if (!_fcChart) { _fcBuildChart(data); return; }
    // Label-keyed: NFL charts carry no Goals Distribution dataset, so index
    // positions are not stable across sports.
    _fcChart.data.datasets.forEach(function(ds) {
      if (ds.label === 'Turf Score') ds.data = data.map(function(d) { return d.twoLine ? null : d.mult; });
      else if (ds.label === 'Turf Score · bye line') ds.data = data.map(function(d) { return d.twoLine ? d.mult : null; });
      else if (ds.label === 'Goals Distribution') ds.data = data.map(function(d) { return d.goals; });
      else if (ds.label === 'DK Expectation') ds.data = data.map(function(d) { return d.teamTotal; });
    });
    // A scale change moves the turf window's bottom anchor (top stays pinned
    // to the DK maximum), so the NFL axis windows recompute on every update.
    var windows = _fcNflAxisWindows(data, multScale);
    if (windows) {
      _fcChart.options.scales.y.min = windows.tMin;
      _fcChart.options.scales.y.max = windows.tMax;
      _fcChart.options.scales.y2.min = windows.y2Min;
      _fcChart.options.scales.y2.max = windows.y2Max;
    }
    _fcChart.update('none');
    _fcUpdateRankList(A, lineExp, probExp, multBase, multScale);
  }

  // Reorder _fcMatchups to match current DOM order, then refresh chart
  function _fcSyncOrder() {
    var items = document.querySelectorAll('.sortable-item');
    var byId = {};
    _fcMatchups.forEach(function(m) { byId[m.emoji + m.team] = m; });
    var reordered = [];
    items.forEach(function(item) {
      var emoji = item.querySelector('.text-lg').textContent.trim();
      var name = item.querySelector('.text-heading').textContent.trim();
      var match = byId[emoji + name];
      if (match) reordered.push(match);
    });
    if (reordered.length === _fcMatchups.length) _fcMatchups = reordered;
    // Trigger chart refresh using current slider values
    _fcUpdate(_fcSliders.A, _fcSliders.lineExp, _fcSliders.probExp, _fcSliders.multBase, _fcSliders.multScale, _fcSliders.goalBase, _fcSliders.goalScale);
  }

  function _fcUpdateRankList(A, lineExp, probExp, multBase, multScale) {
    var items = document.querySelectorAll('.sortable-item');
    var N = items.length;
    var lnN = Math.log(N);
    items.forEach(function(item, i) {
      var rank = i + 1;
      var mult = _fcMult(rank, N, multScale, parseFloat(item.dataset.gameFactor) || 1.0);
      // A null means the table had no cell; leave the stored price on screen
      // rather than printing "NaNx" or a number nobody computed.
      if (mult !== null) item.querySelector('.turf-score-display').textContent = mult.toFixed(1) + 'x';
    });
  }

  // Alpine component — register on alpine:init (deferred Alpine hasn't loaded yet)
  function _fcRegisterAlpine() {
    Alpine.data('formulaCurves', function() {
      return {
        A: _fcSliders.A, lineExp: _fcSliders.lineExp, probExp: _fcSliders.probExp,
        multBase: _fcSliders.multBase, multScale: _fcSliders.multScale,
        goalBase: _fcSliders.goalBase, goalScale: _fcSliders.goalScale,
        refresh() {
          _fcUpdate(this.A, this.lineExp, this.probExp, this.multBase, this.multScale, this.goalBase, this.goalScale);
        },
        init() {
          _fcChart = null;
          _fcLastData = _fcCompute(this.A, this.lineExp, this.probExp, this.multBase, this.multScale, this.goalBase, this.goalScale);
          _fcBuildChart(_fcLastData);
        }
      };
    });
  }

  // Initial load: Alpine hasn't loaded yet (defer), register via alpine:init
  document.addEventListener('alpine:init', _fcRegisterAlpine);

  // Turbo navigation: Alpine is already loaded, register immediately + build chart
  if (typeof Alpine !== 'undefined') {
    _fcRegisterAlpine();
    _fcChart = null;
    _fcLastData = _fcCompute(_fcSliders.A, _fcSliders.lineExp, _fcSliders.probExp, _fcSliders.multBase, _fcSliders.multScale, _fcSliders.goalBase, _fcSliders.goalScale);
    // Build after DOM settles
    setTimeout(function() { _fcBuildChart(_fcLastData); }, 50);
  }

  // Rebuild chart on theme toggle so colors update
  new MutationObserver(function() {
    if (_fcLastData && _fcLastData.length) { _fcBuildChart(_fcLastData); }
  }).observe(document.documentElement, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['class'] });
</script>

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-8 px-2">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-6">
    <div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-heading">Slate Rankings</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-secondary mt-1"><%= @slate.name %></p>
    </div>
    <%= link_to "Back to Contest", root_path,
      class: "text-primary hover:text-primary-300 text-sm font-medium underline underline-offset-2" %>
  </div>

  <!-- Slate tab selector -->
  <% if @slates.size > 1 %>
    <%# flex-wrap + whitespace-nowrap: a plain `flex` row squeezed ~30 pills until
        each one wrapped onto three lines. Let the ROW wrap instead and keep every
        pill on one line. %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-6">
      <% @slates.each do |slate| %>
        <% active = slate.id == @slate.id %>
        <%= link_to "#{slate.sport_emoji} #{slate.selector_label}", slate_path(slate),
          class: "px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-sm font-semibold whitespace-nowrap transition-all #{active ? 'bg-primary text-white' : 'bg-surface-alt text-secondary hover:text-heading'}" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <!-- Formula Curves Chart + Controls -->
  <div x-data="formulaCurves()" x-cloak class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading mb-4">Turf Score Formula</h2>
    <div class="bg-surface border border-subtle rounded-lg p-4" style="position: relative; height: 360px;">
      <canvas id="formulaCurvesChart"></canvas>
    </div>

    <!-- Formula Variables -->
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading mb-4 mt-8">Formula Variables</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <!-- Multiplier -->
      <div class="bg-surface border border-subtle rounded-lg p-4" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--fc-mult);">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-sm font-bold text-heading">Turf Score</span>
          <span class="text-muted text-sm"> = </span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm" style="color: var(--fc-mult-ink)">1.0</span>
          <span class="text-muted text-sm"> + </span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm" style="color: var(--fc-mult-ink)" x-text="multScale.toFixed(1)"></span>
          <span class="text-muted text-sm"> &times; <%= @slate.sport == "nfl" ? "(rank − 1) / (N − 1)" : "ln(rank) / ln(N)" %></span>
        </div>
        <%# Two lines on a bye span (Slate "Two lines"): stated where the formula
            is, so the 1.5x rows in the list below are not read as a bug. %>
        <% if @team_rows.any? { |row| row.game_factor > 1 } %>
          <p class="text-xs text-secondary mb-3" data-testid="two-line-note">
            Two lines: every team ranks on DK points <span class="font-semibold">per game</span>. A team with a bye in this span plays
            <%= @slate.games_per_team - 1 %> of <%= @slate.games_per_team %> games and rides the bye line &mdash; the same curve
            <span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--fc-mult-ink)">&times; <%= number_with_precision(Slate.game_factor(@slate.games_per_team, @slate.games_per_team - 1), precision: 1) %></span>,
            so two games at the bye price score what three would at the full-span price.
          </p>
        <% end %>
        <%# Base is pinned — rank 1 always prices x1.0; only the top end flexes. %>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div>
            <label class="text-xs text-muted block mb-1">Base <span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--fc-mult-ink)">1.0</span> <span class="text-muted">(pinned — rank 1 is always x1.0)</span></label>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="text-xs text-muted block mb-1">Scale <span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--fc-mult-ink)" x-text="multScale.toFixed(1)"></span></label>
            <input type="range" min="0" max="10" step="0.5" x-model.number="multScale" @input="refresh()" class="w-full" style="accent-color: var(--fc-mult);">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Goals are a soccer concept — the card hides on NFL slates. %>
      <% unless @slate.sport == "nfl" %>
        <!-- Goals Distribution -->
        <div class="bg-surface border border-subtle rounded-lg p-4" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--fc-goals);">
          <div class="mb-3">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-heading">Goals Distribution</span>
            <span class="text-muted text-sm"> = </span>
            <span class="font-mono text-sm" style="color: var(--fc-goals-ink)" x-text="goalBase.toFixed(1)"></span>
            <span class="text-muted text-sm"> + </span>
            <span class="font-mono text-sm" style="color: var(--fc-goals-ink)" x-text="goalScale.toFixed(1)"></span>
            <span class="text-muted text-sm"> &times; ln(N/rank) / ln(N)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div>
              <label class="text-xs text-muted block mb-1">Base <span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--fc-goals-ink)" x-text="goalBase.toFixed(1)"></span></label>
              <input type="range" min="0" max="3" step="0.1" x-model.number="goalBase" @input="refresh()" class="w-full" style="accent-color: var(--fc-goals);">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label class="text-xs text-muted block mb-1">Scale <span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--fc-goals-ink)" x-text="goalScale.toFixed(1)"></span></label>
              <input type="range" min="0" max="10" step="0.5" x-model.number="goalScale" @input="refresh()" class="w-full" style="accent-color: var(--fc-goals);">
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <!-- DK Score -->
      <div class="bg-surface border border-subtle rounded-lg p-4" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--fc-dk-score);">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-sm font-bold text-heading">DK Score</span>
          <span class="text-muted text-sm"> = </span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm" style="color: var(--fc-dk-score-ink)"><span x-text="A.toFixed(2)"></span></span>
          <span class="text-muted text-sm"> &times; line</span><sup class="font-mono text-sm" style="color: var(--fc-dk-score-ink)" x-text="lineExp.toFixed(2)"></sup>
          <span class="text-muted text-sm"> &times; prob</span><sup class="font-mono text-sm" style="color: var(--fc-dk-score-ink)" x-text="probExp.toFixed(2)"></sup>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <div>
            <label class="text-xs text-muted block mb-1">A <span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--fc-dk-score-ink)" x-text="A.toFixed(2)"></span></label>
            <input type="range" min="0" max="5" step="0.05" x-model.number="A" @input="refresh()" class="w-full" style="accent-color: var(--fc-dk-score);">
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="text-xs text-muted block mb-1">Line Exp <span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--fc-dk-score-ink)" x-text="lineExp.toFixed(2)"></span></label>
            <input type="range" min="0" max="3" step="0.02" x-model.number="lineExp" @input="refresh()" class="w-full" style="accent-color: var(--fc-dk-score);">
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="text-xs text-muted block mb-1">Prob Exp <span class="font-mono" style="color: var(--fc-dk-score-ink)" x-text="probExp.toFixed(2)"></span></label>
            <input type="range" min="0" max="3" step="0.02" x-model.number="probExp" @input="refresh()" class="w-full" style="accent-color: var(--fc-dk-score);">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="text-secondary text-sm mb-6">
    Drag teams to set offensive rankings. Rank 1 = best offense (lowest Turf Score x1). Rank 48 = weakest (highest Turf Score x3).
    Higher Turf Score = more points when that team scores. Formula: 1.0 + 2.0 &times; ln(rank) / ln(N)
  </p>

  <div x-data="rankManager()" x-cloak>
    <form @submit.prevent="saveRankings()">
      <div class="mb-4 flex gap-3">
        <button type="button" @click="sortByDkScore()" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg flex-1">
          Sort by DK Score
        </button>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg flex-1">
          Save Rankings
        </button>
        <button type="button" @click="saveMultipliers()" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg flex-1">
          Save Multipliers
        </button>
        <button type="button" @click="saveFormula()" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg flex-1" style="border-color: var(--fc-dk-score); color: var(--fc-dk-score-ink);">
          Save Formula
        </button>
      </div>

      <!-- Column headers -->
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-muted uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">
        <span class="w-8 text-right">Rank</span>
        <span class="text-lg invisible">🏳️</span>
        <span class="flex-1">Team</span>
        <span class="w-12 text-right">Turf</span>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-1" x-ref="sortableList">
        <%# One row per TEAM. A team's DK total is the SUM across every game it
            plays in this slate; its rank comes from DK points PER GAME, and its
            multiplier from that rank on the line its game count puts it on (a
            bye team rides the 1.5x line). A one-week slate has one game per
            team, so this renders exactly as it always did. The drag handle
            carries the team's FIRST matchup id; update_rankings resolves it to
            the team and writes the rank to all of that team's games. %>
        <% @team_rows.each_with_index do |row, i| %>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 bg-surface rounded-lg px-4 py-3 border border-subtle cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing sortable-item"
               data-matchup-id="<%= row.matchups.first.id %>"
               data-team-total="<%= row.expected_points %>"
               data-per-game="<%= row.expected_points_per_game.round(2) %>"
               data-game-factor="<%= row.game_factor %>">
            <span class="font-mono text-muted text-sm w-8 text-right rank-number"><%= row.rank || i + 1 %></span>
            <span class="text-lg"><%= row.team.emoji %></span>
            <div class="flex-1 flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
              <span class="text-heading font-semibold text-sm"><%= row.team.name %></span>
              <% opponents = row.matchups.filter_map { |m| m.opponent_team&.short_name } %>
              <% if opponents.any? %>
                <span class="text-muted text-xs">vs <%= opponents.join(" / ") %></span>
              <% end %>
              <% if row.expected_points.positive? %>
                <span class="text-muted text-xs">DK <%= sprintf('%.1f', row.expected_points) %><% if row.matchups.size > 1 %> · <%= sprintf('%.1f', row.expected_points_per_game) %>/g<% end %></span>
              <% end %>
              <% if row.game_factor > 1 %>
                <span class="ml-1 text-xs font-semibold text-violet-ink whitespace-nowrap" data-testid="bye-line-badge"><%= row.matchups.size %> games · bye line</span>
              <% end %>
            </div>
            <span class="font-mono text-primary text-sm w-12 text-right turf-score-display"><%= row.turf_score ? sprintf('%.1f', row.turf_score) : '—' %>x</span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 flex gap-3">
        <button type="button" @click="sortByDkScore()" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg flex-1">
          Sort by DK Score
        </button>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg flex-1">
          Save Rankings
        </button>
        <button type="button" @click="saveMultipliers()" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg flex-1">
          Save Multipliers
        </button>
        <button type="button" @click="saveFormula()" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg flex-1" style="border-color: var(--fc-dk-score); color: var(--fc-dk-score-ink);">
          Save Formula
        </button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/sortablejs@1.15.6/Sortable.min.js"></script>
<script>
  function rankManager() {
    return {
      slateSlug: '<%= @slate.slug %>',
      csrfToken: document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]')?.content,

      init() {
        const list = this.$refs.sortableList;
        Sortable.create(list, {
          animation: 150,
          ghostClass: 'opacity-30',
          onEnd: () => { this.updateNumbers(); _fcSyncOrder(); }
        });
      },

      updateNumbers() {
        const items = this.$refs.sortableList.querySelectorAll('.sortable-item');
        items.forEach((item, i) => {
          item.querySelector('.rank-number').textContent = i + 1;
        });
        _fcUpdateRankList(_fcSliders.A, _fcSliders.lineExp, _fcSliders.probExp, _fcSliders.multBase, _fcSliders.multScale);
      },

      async saveRankings() {
        const items = this.$refs.sortableList.querySelectorAll('.sortable-item');
        const ids = Array.from(items).map(item => item.dataset.matchupId);

        const form = document.createElement('form');
        form.method = 'POST';
        form.action = `/slates/${this.slateSlug}/update_rankings`;

        const methodInput = document.createElement('input');
        methodInput.type = 'hidden';
        methodInput.name = '_method';
        methodInput.value = 'patch';
        form.appendChild(methodInput);

        const csrfInput = document.createElement('input');
        csrfInput.type = 'hidden';
        csrfInput.name = 'authenticity_token';
        csrfInput.value = this.csrfToken;
        form.appendChild(csrfInput);

        ids.forEach(id => {
          const input = document.createElement('input');
          input.type = 'hidden';
          input.name = 'matchup_ids[]';
          input.value = id;
          form.appendChild(input);
        });

        document.body.appendChild(form);
        form.submit();
      },

      sortByDkScore() {
        const list = this.$refs.sortableList;
        const items = Array.from(list.querySelectorAll('.sortable-item'));
        // Per game, not the span total — the order the server ranks on, so a
        // bye team is sorted by strength rather than sunk by its missing game.
        function dkExpectation(el) {
          return parseFloat(el.dataset.perGame) || 0;
        }
        items.sort((a, b) => dkExpectation(b) - dkExpectation(a));
        items.forEach(item => list.appendChild(item));
        this.updateNumbers();
        _fcSyncOrder();
      },

      async saveFormula() {
        const s = _fcSliders;
        const form = document.createElement('form');
        form.method = 'POST';
        form.action = `/slates/${this.slateSlug}/update_formula`;

        const fields = {
          '_method': 'patch',
          'authenticity_token': this.csrfToken,
          'formula_a': s.A,
          'formula_line_exp': s.lineExp,
          'formula_prob_exp': s.probExp,
          'formula_mult_base': s.multBase,
          'formula_mult_scale': s.multScale,
          'formula_goal_base': s.goalBase,
          'formula_goal_scale': s.goalScale
        };

        Object.entries(fields).forEach(([name, value]) => {
          const input = document.createElement('input');
          input.type = 'hidden';
          input.name = name;
          input.value = value;
          form.appendChild(input);
        });

        document.body.appendChild(form);
        form.submit();
      },

      async saveMultipliers() {
        const items = this.$refs.sortableList.querySelectorAll('.sortable-item');

        const form = document.createElement('form');
        form.method = 'POST';
        form.action = `/slates/${this.slateSlug}/update_turf_scores`;

        const methodInput = document.createElement('input');
        methodInput.type = 'hidden';
        methodInput.name = '_method';
        methodInput.value = 'patch';
        form.appendChild(methodInput);

        const csrfInput = document.createElement('input');
        csrfInput.type = 'hidden';
        csrfInput.name = 'authenticity_token';
        csrfInput.value = this.csrfToken;
        form.appendChild(csrfInput);

        items.forEach((item, i) => {
          const id = item.dataset.matchupId;
          const turfScore = item.querySelector('.turf-score-display').textContent.replace('x', '');

          const idInput = document.createElement('input');
          idInput.type = 'hidden';
          idInput.name = `turf_scores[][id]`;
          idInput.value = id;
          form.appendChild(idInput);

          const turfScoreInput = document.createElement('input');
          turfScoreInput.type = 'hidden';
          turfScoreInput.name = `turf_scores[][turf_score]`;
          turfScoreInput.value = turfScore;
          form.appendChild(turfScoreInput);
        });

        document.body.appendChild(form);
        form.submit();
      }
    };
  }
</script>
